OUT INVESTIGATION.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## I'm submitting a...\r\n<!-- Check one of the following options with \"x\" -->\r\n<pre><code>\r\n[ ] Regression (a behavior that used to work and stopped working in a new release)\r\n[x] Bug report  <!-- Please search GitHub for a similar issue or PR before submitting -->\r\n[ ] Feature request\r\n[ ] Documentation issue or request\r\n[ ] Support request => Please do not submit support request here, instead see https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#question\r\n</code></pre>\r\n\r\n## Current behavior\r\nWith InjectionToken\r\n\r\n    export const MY_SYMBOL = new InjectionToken<Symbol>('mySymbol');\r\n\r\nproviding Symbol as value\r\n\r\n    {\r\n      provide: MY_SYMBOL,\r\n      useValue: Symbol('mySymbol')\r\n    }\r\n\r\nthrows error\r\n\r\nchrome\r\n> Cannot create property '__anonymousType' on symbol 'Symbol(mySymbol)'\r\n\r\nedge\r\n> Assignment to read-only properties is not allowed in strict mode\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior\r\nProvides symbol by token.\r\n\r\n## Minimal reproduction of the problem with instructions\r\nhttps://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-xi8mdw\r\n\r\n## What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?\r\nProviding unique symbol\r\n\r\n## Environment\r\n\r\n<pre><code>\r\nAngular version: 5.2.8\r\n<!-- Check whether this is still an issue in the most recent Angular version -->\r\n\r\nBrowser:\r\n- [x] Chrome (desktop) version 65\r\n- [ ] IE version 11 (works surprisingly)\r\n- [x] Edge version 41\r\n \r\nFor Tooling issues:\r\n- Node version: 9.8.0  <!-- run `node --version` -->\r\n- Platform:  Windows \r\n</code></pre>\r\n\r\nSame error as https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/13314 but this is providing a symbol with an InjectionToken not using symbol as a token.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/23170/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"h